<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<meta name="generator" content="toolkit_engine {{ foundation_version }}">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<style>
{{ font_faces }}
:root {
{{ tokens }}
}
{{ components }}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header class="masthead">
  <div>
    <div class="masthead__eyebrow">Tool guide</div>
    <div>{{ display_name }} pyRevit tools</div>
  </div>
  <img src="{{ wordmark_inverse }}" alt="{{ logo_alt }}">
</header>
<main>
  <p class="label">{{ tab }} / {{ panel }}</p>
  <h1>Hello Button</h1>
  <p class="lede">A deliberately small, read-only reference tool. It confirms the
  extension loaded and demonstrates project-context validation before any UI.</p>
  <p><span class="badge badge--success">{{ badge_success }}</span><span class="badge badge--info">{{ badge_info }}</span></p>

  <h2>Use it</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open a Revit project document.</li>
    <li>On the <strong>{{ tab }}</strong> tab, in the <strong>{{ panel }}</strong> panel, click <strong>Hello Button</strong>.</li>
    <li>Review the project title, active view, and non-template view count.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>With no document open the tool exits quietly. In a family document it explains that a project is required.</p>

  <h2>Technical design</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Document context</th><td>Active Revit project document</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Revit API query</th><td><code>FilteredElementCollector(doc).OfClass(DB.View)</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Interface</th><td><code>pyrevit.forms.alert</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Transactions</th><td>None. The tool never modifies the model or linked documents.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Minimum pyRevit</th><td>4.8.10</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Interface specimen</h2>
  <p class="small">How {{ short_name }} components render in web surfaces. The native WPF specimen is verified separately.</p>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="label">Buttons</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Run audit</button>
      <button class="btn btn--secondary" type="button">Preview</button>
      <button class="btn btn--secondary is-focus-depicted" type="button">Keyboard focus</button>
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" disabled>Unavailable</button>
      <button class="btn btn--secondary" type="button" disabled>Unavailable</button>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Registration marks: {{ marks_note }}. Keyboard focus is depicted on the third button; press Tab to see the live ring.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="label">Selection</p>
    <div class="chips">
      <button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="true">Floor plans</button>
      <button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Sections</button>
      <button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Sheets</button>
    </div>
    <ul class="list" role="listbox" aria-label="Views">
      <li role="option" aria-selected="false">Level 01 - Floor Plan</li>
      <li role="option" aria-selected="true">Level 02 - Floor Plan (selected)</li>
      <li role="option" aria-selected="false">Roof - Floor Plan</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="label">Status badges</p>
    <span class="badge badge--info">{{ badge_info }}</span><span class="badge badge--success">{{ badge_success }}</span><span class="badge badge--warning">{{ badge_warning }}</span><span class="badge badge--danger">{{ badge_danger }}</span>
  </div>

  <h2>Support</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Support</th><td><a href="{{ support_url }}">{{ support_url }}</a></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Documentation</th><td>{{ documentation }}</td></tr>
  </table>
</main>
<footer>
  <img src="{{ symbol_light }}" alt="{{ logo_alt }}">
  <span>Generated by toolkit_engine {{ foundation_version }}. Licences and notices: <a href="{{ notices_href }}">THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</a>.</span>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
